refactor the multi pane explorer implementation.

the multi pane explorer is one of two options
the user can select to be the 'hub' or central
point of the users experience with Richards File Utilities(rfu).

the user will be given the option with a small button to (quick)change to the tabbed interface and back.

by default multi pane explorer shall open with 4 parallel panes, no fall back.

the left pane will be tabbed, 'Bookmarks', 'Recent' and 'Tools'.  
The 'Recent' tab will be seleceted as default.
The default may be changed by the user
The 'Bookmarks' tab will display in the top half of the pane the 'Tools' which the user has bookmarked,
the bottom half of the display drives, folders or network location the user has bookmarked
The 'Recent' tab will display in the top half of the pane the last 
The 'Tools' tab will display all the programs (only executables not the folders) of Richards File Utilities(rfu)

the two center panes shall display the files, directories and network locations for the user.
At the top the user can select with drop down button the local and attached storage
by default the root drive will be displayed, which can be changed by the user
the user shall be able to select between 1,2,3 and 4 panes.
when the user selects 1 pane the layout option will be disabled
when the user selects 2 panes, the layout option will allow horizontal and vertical arrangement of two center panes
when the user selects 3 panes, the layout option will allow horizontal, vertical and grid arrangement of two center panes
when the user selects 4 panes, the layout option will allow horizontal, vertical and grid arrangement of two center panes

the right pane will be tabbed, 'Preview' and 'Properties'
the right pane will display the preview of the left tab
by default may be cahnged by the user to be either 'Preview' or 'Properties'